Hi, `ngfactory` are only created when using NGC, Ivy uses a different compiler (NGTSC) which doesn't generate factories.

Which means you need to remove the factory references. 
Ie from
```ts
import {platformBrowser} from '@angular/platform-browser';
import {AppModuleNgFactory} from './application.module.ngfactory';

platformBrowser()
    .bootstrapModuleFactory(AppModuleNgFactory)
    .catch(e => console.error('Application bootstrap failed', e));
```

to
```ts
import {platformBrowser} from '@angular/platform-browser';
import {AppModule} from './application.module';

platformBrowser()
    .bootstrapModule(AppModule)
    .catch(e => console.error('Application bootstrap failed', e));
```

Alternatively you can enable factory shims by adding `"allowEmptyCodegenFiles": true` under `angularCompilerOptions` in your `tsconfig.json`. However it's worth mentioning that the later is not recommended.

